      "teacher_walkthrough": [
        "Write down the variance formula for a binomial random variable $X \\sim \\mathrm{B}(n, p)$:\n$$\\operatorname{Var}(X) = npq = np(1 - p)$$\nFrom part (i), $n = 30$ and $p = 0.207$, so $q = 1 - 0.207 = 0.793$.\nSubstitute these values:\n$$\\operatorname{Var}(X) = 30 \\times 0.207 \\times 0.793 = 6.21 \\times 0.793 = 4.92453 \\approx 4.92$$"
