      "hints": [
        "Define the new binomial distribution for 15 throws: $Y \\sim \\mathrm{B}(15, 0.207)$.",
        "Use the complement rule: $\\mathrm{P}(Y \\ge 2) = 1 - \\mathrm{P}(Y = 0) - \\mathrm{P}(Y = 1)$.",
        "Calculate $\\mathrm{P}(Y = 0) = (0.793)^{15}$ and $\\mathrm{P}(Y = 1) = \\binom{15}{1}(0.207)(0.793)^{14}$, and subtract from 1."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Model the number of $4$s in $15$ throws as $Y \\sim \\mathrm{B}(15, 0.207)$:\n$$\\mathrm{P}(Y \\ge 2) = 1 - \\mathrm{P}(Y = 0) - \\mathrm{P}(Y = 1)$$",
        "Calculate the individual binomial terms:\n$$\\mathrm{P}(Y = 0) = (0.793)^{15} \\approx 0.030807$$\n$$\\mathrm{P}(Y = 1) = \\binom{15}{1} (0.207)^1 (0.793)^{14} = 15(0.207)(0.793)^{14} \\approx 0.120625$$",
        "Subtract from $1$:\n$$\\mathrm{P}(Y \\ge 2) = 1 - (0.030807 + 0.120625) = 1 - 0.151432 = 0.848568 \\approx 0.848$$"
      ],
