      "teacher_walkthrough": [
        "Step 1: Set up the binomial model for $15$ throws.\nLet $Y$ be the number of $4$s obtained in $n = 15$ throws:\n$$Y \\sim \\mathrm{B}(15, 0.207)$$\nwhere $q = 1 - 0.207 = 0.793$.",
        "Step 2: Express the required event using the complement rule:\n$$\\mathrm{P}(Y \\ge 2) = 1 - \\mathrm{P}(Y < 2) = 1 - [\\mathrm{P}(Y = 0) + \\mathrm{P}(Y = 1)]$$",
        "Step 3: Evaluate $\\mathrm{P}(Y = 0)$ and $\\mathrm{P}(Y = 1)$:\n$$\\mathrm{P}(Y = 0) = \\binom{15}{0} (0.207)^0 (0.793)^{15} = (0.793)^{15} \\approx 0.030807$$\n$$\\mathrm{P}(Y = 1) = \\binom{15}{1} (0.207)^1 (0.793)^{14} = 15 \\times 0.207 \\times (0.793)^{14} \\approx 0.120625$$",
        "Step 4: Sum the lower tail probabilities:\n$$\\mathrm{P}(Y = 0) + \\mathrm{P}(Y = 1) = 0.030807 + 0.120625 = 0.151432$$",
        "Step 5: Subtract from $1$:\n$$\\mathrm{P}(Y \\ge 2) = 1 - 0.151432 = 0.848568 \\approx 0.848$$"
